   under starvation stress conditions},
Journal = {JOURNAL OF MOLECULAR EVOLUTION},
Year = {1998},
Volume = {47},
Number = {3},
Pages = {363-368},
Month = {SEP},
Abstract = {A novel system to study the evolution of transcription signals in
   heterologous systems under selective starvation conditions is described.
   It is based on the plasmid-mediated transfer of his biosynthetic genes
   from Azospirillum brasilense into a heterologous Escherichia coli mutant
   population lacking histidine biosynthetic ability. We show that under
   highly selective stressful conditions, genetic changes in the donor
   plasmid lead to mutated sequences that are efficiently recognized as
   promoters by the E. coli RNA polymerase.},
