Month = {JUN 15},
Abstract = {A model for the transmission of dengue fever in a constant human
   population and variable vector population is discussed. A complete
   global analysis is given, which uses the results of the theory of
   competitive systems and stability of periodic orbits, to establish the
   global stability of the endemic equilibrium. The control measures of the
   vector population are discussed in terms of the threshold condition,
   which governs the existence and stability of the endemic equilibrium.
