Organization = {US Natl Sci Fdn; NASA; USAF, Off Sci Res; Duke Univ},
Abstract = {Avalanches in a two-dimensional dry granular system, the rotating drum
   setup, are studied in detail. The distribution of angles at which
   avalanches initiate and terminate, as well as those for time between
   avalanches, are characterized. The results are analyzed assuming that
   the instantaneous surface angle of the pile is a stochastic Markov
   process. The macroscopic evolution equations for the average angle of
   the pile and its standard deviation are also studied. We comment on
   other variations of the experimental setup, such as having different
   effective gravity force.},
