   Superconductivity - High Temperature Superconductors IV (M2S-HTSC IV),
   GRENOBLE, FRANCE, JUL 05-09, 1994},
Organization = {EUROPEAN COMMUNITY; MINIST EDUC \& SCI, FRANCE; CNRS; FRENCH NATL CTR
   SCI RES; RHONE ALPES REG; CITY GRENOBLE},
Abstract = {A model with quasi-normal occupancy is applied to several typical
   high-T-c superconductors obtaining tighter-bound Cooper fermion pairs.
   Within this model a small energy gap of the order of the Debye energy
   near the Fermi surface is proposed. An important physical requirement of
   the model is that the anomaly in the occupancy occurs simultaneously to
   the pair formation. The role of the variation of the ratio R = 2
   Delta(0)/kT(c) in the range 2 - 10 is studied. The phonon barrier can be
   overcomed and then obtain a good description of high-T-c superconductor
   cuprates in all the range of values for R suggested by experimental
   results.},
