   ENDOCRINOLOGY},
Year = {1993},
Volume = {106},
Number = {3},
Pages = {761-764},
Month = {NOV},
Abstract = {1. The oxygen consumption rates of C. idella decrease when exposed to
   nitrite but return to normal in the presence of chloride, reaching
   similar values to those of the control groups. 2. A quadratic polynomial
   model describes the relationship between metabolic rate, wet weight and
   chloride concentration in the environment, both with nitrite fixed
   (cL(50)-96hr=1.71mg N-NO2-/l) as chloride varied (3-6mg/l) and chloride
   fixed (3mg/l) as nitrite varied from lethal to sublethal concentration
   (1.71, 1.0, 0.5 and 0.3 mg N-NO2-/l). 3. The metabolic rate is a very
   useful indicator of stress caused by nitrite.},
